Alternatively, we can write $P(x) = (x-r)^4$ for some real root $r$. Expanding this, we get $P(x) = x^4 - 4rx^3 + 6r^2 x^2 - 4r^3 x + r^4$. Comparing the coefficients with $P(x) = x^4+kx^3+x^2+4kx+16$, we have:
