\begin{enumerate}
    \item Suppose the four students are labeled $S_1, S_2, S_3, S_4$.
    \item The teacher is randomly guessing which paper belongs to each of the four remaining students. 
    \item Let $X$ be the event that the teacher correctly guesses which paper belongs to each of the four remaining students.
    \item Since the teacher is randomly guessing, each student's paper has an equal chance of being assigned to any of the students. Thus, the probability that the teacher guesses correctly to student $S_i$ is $\frac{1}{4}$ for each $i \in \{1, 2, 3, 4\}$.
    \item The events of guessing correctly for each of the four students are independent.
    \item Thus, the probability that the teacher correctly guesses which paper belongs to each of the four remaining students is
    $$P(X) = \left(\frac{1}{4}\right)^4 = \frac{1}{256}.$$
\end{enumerate}

\boxed{\frac{1}{256}}

